/**
 * The `mask-border-repeat` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
 * specifies how the images for the sides and the middle part of the [mask border
 * image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-border) are
 * scaled and tiled.
 *
 * Initial: stretch. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - repeat: The source image's edge regions are tiled (repeated) to fill the gap between each
 * border. Tiles may be clipped to achieve the proper fit.
 * - round: The source image's edge regions are tiled (repeated) to fill the gap between each
 * border. Tiles may be stretched to achieve the proper fit.
 * - space: The source image's edge regions are tiled (repeated) to fill the gap between each
 * border. Extra space will be distributed in between tiles to achieve the proper fit.
 * - stretch: The source image's edge regions are stretched to fill the gap between each border.
 *
 * Grammar: <'border-image-repeat'>
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-masking-1/#propdef-mask-border-repeat
 *
 * Author guide:
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-border-repeat
 *
